		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: A/B?]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4572&amp;p=34029#p34029"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div>I’m having a tough time saying what I want. <br>My radio is in memory mode. It’s showing an A and B talk group name. For the sake of explanation, the A is showing the IN3118 group and the B is showing North America. I can scroll through both A and B to the different talk groups I have programmed. No matter what I do, it only operates with the talk group on the top line. I’m thinking that hitting the A/B button should switch it to the one on bottom or the B. I do this on all of my non DMR Baofengs. Maybe the DMR just doesn’t work like this or I have some kind of programming error?<br>I tried attaching a picture but couldn’t figure out how. I suspect image size too big but I never got any kind of error message. <br><br>Matt<br>Double clicking the orange button gets into the menu for moving VFO to memory or vice-versa.</div></blockquote>OK, I got you now. OpenGD77 is working in a different way than commercial/traditional DMR. In OpenGD77 the top line is talk group and the bottom line is channel.<br><br>on 1801 radio, you change channel by arrow up/down and change talkgroup with left/right<br>how to write a codeplug is the key. In Traditional DMR you will have to create multiple channel for a repeater. These channels are almost identical, only talk group and sometimes time slot that changed. on the radio, you can only change channels, there is noway to change talkgroup, except manual dial.<br><br>In OpenGD77, we use only one channel per repeater. then create a "talkgroup list" and attach the talkgroup list to the channel. Now on the radio you can change talkgroup.<br><br>Hope this make sense</div></blockquote>Yes!!! That explains it. It also shows me I need to change the way I’m labeling my channels as I was naming the channels the same as the talk groups. That’s why I could have the same name on both lines of the screen or different names. I thought it was like an A and B channel on a regular HT. <br>Thank you for the explanation!<br><br>Matt, NE9D<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=7103">NE9D</a> — Sun Nov 10, 2024 1:37 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
